{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"332","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Maximum Absurdity"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Reforms continue entering Berland. For example, during yesterday sitting the Berland Parliament approved as much as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" laws (each law has been assigned a unique number from 1 to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Today all these laws were put on the table of the President of Berland, G.W. Boosch, to be signed."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This time mr. Boosch plans to sign "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2k"},{"kind":"text","text":" laws. He decided to choose "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly two"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" non-intersecting segments of integers from 1 to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" of length "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" and sign all laws, whose numbers fall into these segments. More formally, mr. Boosch is going to choose two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ a ≤ b ≤ n - k + 1, b - a ≥ k)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and sign all laws with numbers lying in the segments "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[a; a + k - 1]"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[b; b + k - 1]"},{"kind":"text","text":" (borders are included)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As mr. Boosch chooses the laws to sign, he of course considers the public opinion. Allberland Public Opinion Study Centre (APOSC) conducted opinion polls among the citizens, processed the results into a report and gave it to the president. The report contains the absurdity value for each law, in the public opinion. As mr. Boosch is a real patriot, he is keen on signing the laws with the maximum total absurdity. Help him."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 2·105"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 < 2k ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of laws accepted by the parliament and the length of one segment in the law list, correspondingly. The next line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1, x2, ..., xn"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the absurdity of each law ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ xi ≤ 109)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the beginning of segments that mr. Boosch should choose. That means that the president signs laws with numbers from segments "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[a; a + k - 1]"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[b; b + k - 1]"},{"kind":"text","text":". If there are multiple solutions, print the one with the minimum number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":". If there still are multiple solutions, print the one with the minimum "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 2\n3 6 1 1 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6 2\n1 1 1 1 1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample mr. Boosch signs laws with numbers from segments [1;2] and [4;5]. The total absurdity of the signed laws equals "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 + 6 + 1 + 6 = 16"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample mr. Boosch signs laws with numbers from segments [1;2] and [3;4]. The total absurdity of the signed laws equals "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 4"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"332B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/332/problem/B"}